---
title: Pasta alla zozzona
servings: 4
tags: [italian, pork]
cuisine: italian
time: 40 minutes
source: Pasta alla zozzona by GialloZafferano, https://www.giallozafferano.com/recipes/pasta-alla-zozzona-carbonara-amatriciana-and-cacio-e-pepe-pasta.html
---

Put a #large pot{} of water on to boil and salt it.

Cut the @guanciale{200%g} into strips. Squeeze the @Italian sausage{250%g}(pork)
out of its casing and break it into chunks.

Drizzle a #wide pan{} with @olive oil{}(extra virgin), add the guanciale and
sausage, and brown over medium-low heat ~{15%minutes}, stirring now and then.

Add the @cherry tomatoes{350%g}(canned), cover, and cook ~{10%minutes}.

In a #bowl{}, stir the @egg yolks{4}(medium) with 60 g of the
@Pecorino Romano{100%g}(grated) to a thick cream.

Cook the @dried pasta{320%g}(rigatoni). Loosen the yolk cream with a ladle of
the pasta water.

Drain the pasta just al dente, tip it into the sauce, toss well and take the pan
off the heat. Stir in the yolk cream, then the last 40 g of Pecorino, and serve.

> Off the heat is the whole trick: the yolks should thicken into a sauce, not
> scramble.
